            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "AI findings, feel free to ignore these if they are known issues / planned followups.\r\n\r\n<details>\r\n<summary>AI findings</summary>\r\n\r\n1. **Assert crash on a truncated multibyte char** (`src/nvim/mbyte.c:1871`)\r\n   - When the length limit cuts off the next char, `utf_ClusterInfo_impl` returns `.len = next_len` instead of 1. The next `utf_ClusterInfo_len` call then pushes `*size` negative and calls the impl with `*max_len <= 0`.\r\n   - `nvim --clean --headless -c 'call setreg(\"a\", \"a\\xe2\\n\\xc3\\xa9\", \"b\")'` aborts with `Assertion failed: (*next >= 0x80 && *max_len > 0), function utf_ClusterInfo_impl`. Base returns `^V2`.\r\n   - With asserts compiled out, it reads 2 bytes past the NUL terminator.\r\n\r\n2. **ASCII + SpacingMark is drawn as `>`** (`src/nvim/grid.c:451`)\r\n   - `grid_line_puts` now takes its width from the cluster, so `a` + U+0903 is 2 cells. Callers still advance by `utf_ptr2cells()`, which returns 1 for any ASCII lead byte, so the second cell gets overwritten.\r\n   - `:echo \"a\\u0903\"` shows `>` (base: `aः`),  and `:echo \"xa\\u0903b\"` shows `x>b` (base: `xaःb`).\r\n   - Both `msg_puts_display` and `pum_grid_puts_with_attrs` get out of step this way.\r\n\r\n3. **An illegal byte counts as 1 cell instead of 4** (`src/nvim/mbyte.h:189`)\r\n   - The fast paths in `utf_ClusterInfo_len` use `utf_char2cells(cur.chr.value)`, which returns 1 for any value below 0x80, including -1.\r\n   - `nvim_open_win(..., {border={\"\\255\"}})` used to fail with \"expected only one-cell chars\" and now succeeds.\r\n   - `setreg('d', \"\\xffx\\nb\", 'b')` gives `^V2` (base: `^V5`).\r\n\r\n4. **A control char's width depends on the next byte** (`src/nvim/mbyte.c:1856`)\r\n   - The fast paths use `utf_char2cells` (1 cell), but when the next byte is non-ASCII the impl uses `basechar_cells_impl` (`dy_escape_width`).\r\n   - `setreg('c', \"\\tä\\nb\", 'b')` gives `^V3` (base: `^V2`), while `\"\\ta\"` still counts the tab as 1 cell.\r\n   - `mb_string2cells` and `mb_string2cells_len` now disagree on the same text (ext-messages `msg_col` at `message.c:2445`).\r\n\r\n5. **`grid_line_puts` reads past `textlen`** (`src/nvim/grid.c:454`)\r\n   - The base clamp `if (mbyte_blen > maxlen) mbyte_blen = 1` was removed.\r\n   - `grid_line_puts(col, \"a\\xe2\\x82\\xac\", 3, attr)` builds the schar from all 3 bytes of `€`, one byte past `textlen`. The glyph is drawn whole, and the read goes past the end of a buffer that isn't NUL-terminated.\r\n\r\n6. **Blockwise register width stops at an embedded NUL** (`src/nvim/register.c:2651`)\r\n   - `str_to_reg` now uses `mb_string2cells_len`, which stops at the first NUL. The old loop stepped over NULs, counting each as 1 cell.\r\n   - `\"ab\\0cdef\"` (via `write_reg_contents_ex` with a length) gets `y_width` 2 instead of 6.\r\n\r\n7. **Debug builds abort on register lines longer than `INT_MAX` bytes** (`src/nvim/mbyte.c:619`)\r\n   - `mb_string2cells_len` casts its `size_t` length to `int`, so a huge length wraps negative and trips the new `assert(size >= 0)` in `utf_ptr2CharInfo_len`. Base returned a wrong but harmless width.\r\n\r\n</details>",
